*> The server pack cache (US18-8; 08 §9.3, §9.4): <game directory>/downloads/<pack UUID>/<lowercase
*> hex SHA-1 of the content>. PACK-SHA1 hashes bytes (a direct call of OpenSSL EVP_Digest with
*> EVP_sha1, research R10); PACK-CACHE-FIND reuses a cached file whose content still has the
*> expected hash; PACK-CACHE-STORE keeps a downloaded file; PACK-CACHE-VACUUM keeps at most 20 cached
*> files at start-up, removing the oldest first (08 §9.4 housekeeping). The event log downloads/
*> log.json of 08 §9.4 is not written: nothing reads it.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. PACK-SHA1.
*> USING area, length (BINARY-LONG), hex out (PIC X(40)): the lowercase hex SHA-1 of the bytes.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 01 WS-LENGTH              BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
 01 WS-DIGEST              PIC X(64).
 01 WS-DIGEST-LENGTH       BINARY-LONG UNSIGNED.
 01 WS-ALGORITHM           USAGE POINTER.
 01 WS-ENGINE              USAGE POINTER VALUE NULL.
 01 WS-RC                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-HEX                 PIC X(16) VALUE "0123456789abcdef".
 01 WS-I                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-B                   BINARY-LONG.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 01 L-AREA                 PIC X.
 01 L-LENGTH               BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-HEX                  PIC X(40).
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING L-AREA L-LENGTH L-HEX.
     MOVE L-LENGTH TO WS-LENGTH
     CALL STATIC "EVP_sha1" RETURNING WS-ALGORITHM
     CALL STATIC "EVP_Digest" USING BY REFERENCE L-AREA BY VALUE WS-LENGTH
         BY REFERENCE WS-DIGEST BY REFERENCE WS-DIGEST-LENGTH BY VALUE WS-ALGORITHM
         BY VALUE WS-ENGINE RETURNING WS-RC
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 20
         COMPUTE WS-B = FUNCTION ORD(WS-DIGEST(WS-I:1)) - 1
         MOVE WS-HEX(WS-B / 16 + 1:1) TO L-HEX(WS-I * 2 - 1:1)
         MOVE WS-HEX(FUNCTION MOD(WS-B, 16) + 1:1) TO L-HEX(WS-I * 2:1)
     END-PERFORM
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM PACK-SHA1.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. PACK-CACHE-PATH.
*> USING CLIENT-STATE, pack UUID (PIC X(16)), hash (PIC X(40)) or spaces, path out (PIC X(1100)),
*> length out: downloads/<uuid>/<hash>, or the directory downloads/<uuid> for spaces.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 01 WS-UUID                PIC X(36).
 01 WS-UUID-LENGTH         BINARY-LONG.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 01 L-UUID                 PIC X(16).
 01 L-HASH                 PIC X(40).
 01 L-PATH                 PIC X(1100).
 01 L-LENGTH               BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING CLIENT-STATE L-UUID L-HASH L-PATH L-LENGTH.
     CALL "UUID-TEXT" USING L-UUID WS-UUID WS-UUID-LENGTH
     MOVE SPACES TO L-PATH
     STRING CL-GAME-DIR(1:CL-GAME-DIR-LENGTH) "/downloads/" WS-UUID DELIMITED BY SIZE
         INTO L-PATH
     COMPUTE L-LENGTH = CL-GAME-DIR-LENGTH + 47
     IF L-HASH NOT = SPACES
         MOVE "/" TO L-PATH(L-LENGTH + 1:1)
         MOVE L-HASH TO L-PATH(L-LENGTH + 2:40)
         ADD 41 TO L-LENGTH
     END-IF
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM PACK-CACHE-PATH.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. PACK-CACHE-FIND.
*> USING CLIENT-STATE, server pack row, found out: with an expected hash, a cached file at
*> <uuid>/<hash> whose content hashes to it is the pack's file (RP-FILE), found 1 (08 §9.4).
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 01 WS-PATH                PIC X(1100).
 01 WS-LENGTH              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-SIZE                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CAP                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ZERO                BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-STATUS              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-DUMMY               PIC X.
 01 WS-ADDR                USAGE POINTER.
 01 WS-HEX                 PIC X(40).
 01 B-FILE                 PIC X BASED.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 01 L-ROW                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-FOUND                BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING CLIENT-STATE L-ROW L-FOUND.
     MOVE 0 TO L-FOUND
     IF RP-HASH(L-ROW) = SPACES
         GOBACK
     END-IF
     CALL "PACK-CACHE-PATH" USING CLIENT-STATE RP-UUID(L-ROW) RP-HASH(L-ROW) WS-PATH WS-LENGTH
     CALL "FILE-READ-ALL" USING WS-PATH WS-LENGTH WS-DUMMY WS-ZERO WS-SIZE WS-STATUS
     IF WS-STATUS NOT = 5
         GOBACK
     END-IF
     ALLOCATE WS-SIZE CHARACTERS RETURNING WS-ADDR
     SET ADDRESS OF B-FILE TO WS-ADDR
     MOVE WS-SIZE TO WS-CAP
     CALL "FILE-READ-ALL" USING WS-PATH WS-LENGTH B-FILE WS-CAP WS-SIZE WS-STATUS
     CALL "PACK-SHA1" USING B-FILE WS-SIZE WS-HEX
     FREE WS-ADDR
     IF WS-HEX = RP-HASH(L-ROW)
         MOVE WS-PATH TO RP-FILE(L-ROW)
         MOVE WS-LENGTH TO RP-FILE-LENGTH(L-ROW)
         MOVE 1 TO L-FOUND
     END-IF
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM PACK-CACHE-FIND.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. PACK-CACHE-STORE.
*> USING CLIENT-STATE, server pack row, area, length, hash (PIC X(40), of the bytes): writes the
*> bytes to downloads/<uuid>/<hash>, the pack's file (RP-FILE).
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 01 WS-SPACES              PIC X(40) VALUE SPACES.
 01 WS-PATH                PIC X(1100).
 01 WS-LENGTH              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ACCESS              PIC X COMP-X VALUE 2.
 01 WS-DENY                PIC X COMP-X VALUE 0.
 01 WS-DEVICE              PIC X COMP-X VALUE 0.
 01 WS-HANDLE              PIC X(4).
 01 WS-OFFSET              PIC X(8) COMP-X VALUE 0.
 01 WS-COUNT               PIC X(4) COMP-X.
 01 WS-FLAGS               PIC X COMP-X VALUE 0.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 01 L-ROW                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-AREA                 PIC X.
 01 L-LENGTH               BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-HASH                 PIC X(40).
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING CLIENT-STATE L-ROW L-AREA L-LENGTH L-HASH.
     CALL "PACK-CACHE-PATH" USING CLIENT-STATE RP-UUID(L-ROW) WS-SPACES WS-PATH WS-LENGTH
     CALL "CBL_CREATE_DIR" USING WS-PATH
     CALL "PACK-CACHE-PATH" USING CLIENT-STATE RP-UUID(L-ROW) L-HASH WS-PATH WS-LENGTH
     CALL "CBL_CREATE_FILE" USING WS-PATH WS-ACCESS WS-DENY WS-DEVICE WS-HANDLE
     MOVE L-LENGTH TO WS-COUNT
     CALL "CBL_WRITE_FILE" USING WS-HANDLE WS-OFFSET WS-COUNT WS-FLAGS L-AREA
     CALL "CBL_CLOSE_FILE" USING WS-HANDLE
     MOVE 0 TO RETURN-CODE
     MOVE WS-PATH TO RP-FILE(L-ROW)
     MOVE WS-LENGTH TO RP-FILE-LENGTH(L-ROW)
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM PACK-CACHE-STORE.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. PACK-CACHE-VACUUM.
*> USING CLIENT-STATE: when downloads/ holds more than 20 files (one directory level per pack id,
*> at most 256 files looked at), the oldest by modification time are deleted until 20 remain.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 01 WS-DIRZ                PIC X(1200).
 01 WS-LIST                PIC X(65536).
 01 WS-SUBLIST             PIC X(65536).
 01 WS-CAPACITY            BINARY-LONG VALUE 65536.
 01 WS-COUNT               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-SUBCOUNT            BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-RC                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-PTR                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-SUBPTR              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ENTRY               PIC X(256).
 01 WS-LENGTH              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-SUB                 PIC X(256).
 01 WS-SUBLENGTH           BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-DIR                 PIC X(1200).
 01 WS-DIR-LENGTH          BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-I                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-K                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-OLDEST              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-INFO.
    05 WS-SIZE             PIC X(8) COMP-X.
    05 WS-DAY              PIC X COMP-X.
    05 WS-MONTH            PIC X COMP-X.
    05 WS-YEAR             PIC X(2) COMP-X.
    05 WS-HOUR             PIC X COMP-X.
    05 WS-MINUTE           PIC X COMP-X.
    05 WS-SECOND           PIC X COMP-X.
    05 WS-HUNDREDTH        PIC X COMP-X.
 01 WS-FILES.
    05 WS-FILE-COUNT       BINARY-LONG.
    05 WS-FILE OCCURS 256 TIMES.
       10 WS-F-PATH        PIC X(1200).
       10 WS-F-TIME        BINARY-DOUBLE.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING CLIENT-STATE.
     MOVE 0 TO WS-FILE-COUNT
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-DIR
     STRING CL-GAME-DIR(1:CL-GAME-DIR-LENGTH) "/downloads" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-DIR
     COMPUTE WS-DIR-LENGTH = CL-GAME-DIR-LENGTH + 10
     MOVE LOW-VALUES TO WS-DIRZ
     MOVE WS-DIR(1:WS-DIR-LENGTH) TO WS-DIRZ(1:WS-DIR-LENGTH)
     MOVE 0 TO WS-COUNT
     CALL STATIC "cc_fs_list" USING BY REFERENCE WS-DIRZ BY REFERENCE WS-LIST
         BY VALUE WS-CAPACITY BY REFERENCE WS-COUNT RETURNING WS-RC
     MOVE 1 TO WS-PTR
     PERFORM WS-COUNT TIMES
         MOVE SPACES TO WS-ENTRY
         UNSTRING WS-LIST DELIMITED BY X"0A" INTO WS-ENTRY COUNT IN WS-LENGTH WITH POINTER WS-PTR
         MOVE LOW-VALUES TO WS-DIRZ
         STRING WS-DIR(1:WS-DIR-LENGTH) "/" WS-ENTRY(2:WS-LENGTH - 1) DELIMITED BY SIZE
             INTO WS-DIRZ
         MOVE 0 TO WS-SUBCOUNT
         CALL STATIC "cc_fs_list" USING BY REFERENCE WS-DIRZ BY REFERENCE WS-SUBLIST
             BY VALUE WS-CAPACITY BY REFERENCE WS-SUBCOUNT RETURNING WS-RC
         MOVE 1 TO WS-SUBPTR
         PERFORM WS-SUBCOUNT TIMES
             MOVE SPACES TO WS-SUB
             UNSTRING WS-SUBLIST DELIMITED BY X"0A" INTO WS-SUB COUNT IN WS-SUBLENGTH
                 WITH POINTER WS-SUBPTR
             IF WS-SUB(1:1) = "F" AND WS-FILE-COUNT < 256
                 ADD 1 TO WS-FILE-COUNT
                 MOVE SPACES TO WS-F-PATH(WS-FILE-COUNT)
                 STRING WS-DIR(1:WS-DIR-LENGTH) "/" WS-ENTRY(2:WS-LENGTH - 1) "/"
                     WS-SUB(2:WS-SUBLENGTH - 1) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-F-PATH(WS-FILE-COUNT)
                 CALL "CBL_CHECK_FILE_EXIST" USING WS-F-PATH(WS-FILE-COUNT) WS-INFO
                 COMPUTE WS-F-TIME(WS-FILE-COUNT) = ((((WS-YEAR * 13 + WS-MONTH) * 32 + WS-DAY)
                     * 24 + WS-HOUR) * 60 + WS-MINUTE) * 6000 + WS-SECOND * 100 + WS-HUNDREDTH
             END-IF
         END-PERFORM
     END-PERFORM
     PERFORM VARYING WS-K FROM WS-FILE-COUNT BY -1 UNTIL WS-K <= 20
         MOVE 1 TO WS-OLDEST
         PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 2 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > WS-FILE-COUNT
             IF WS-F-TIME(WS-I) < WS-F-TIME(WS-OLDEST)
                 MOVE WS-I TO WS-OLDEST
             END-IF
         END-PERFORM
         CALL "CBL_DELETE_FILE" USING WS-F-PATH(WS-OLDEST)
         MOVE 999999999999999 TO WS-F-TIME(WS-OLDEST)
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE 0 TO RETURN-CODE
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM PACK-CACHE-VACUUM.
